The ability to think is a clear and distinct mental activity that cannot be doubted, as it is the very act of questioning itself.
Even if all other beliefs are uncertain, the fact that one is doubting implies the existence of a thinking entity, as doubt is a mental state.
The process of doubting itself is a form of thinking, which confirms the presence of a thinking self, making the thinker undeniable.
If one can think, they must exist as a thinking being, as the act of thinking presupposes the existence of the thinker.
The existence of thought is a direct proof of the existence of the thinker, as thought cannot occur without a thinker.